Package: eSVD2
Title: Cohort-Wide Differential Expression for Single-Cell RNA-Seq via
    'eSVD-DE'
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: person("Kevin Z", "Lin", email = "kzlin@uw.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tests for differential expression between case and control
    individuals in single-cell RNA-seq cohorts, where the unit of inference
    is the individual (donor) rather than the cell. A low-rank exponential
    family embedding ('eSVD') pools information across genes to denoise each
    cell's expression, a Gamma-Poisson posterior then re-weights the denoised
    values against the covariate-adjusted sequencing depth so that the
    Type-1 error is not inflated, and a Welch statistic on the
    per-individual posterior means is calibrated with an empirical null.
    The method is described in Lin, Qiu and Roeder (2024)
    <doi:10.1186/s12859-024-05724-7>.
Depends:
    R (>= 3.5.0)
